cff-version: 1.2.0
title: homeroom
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
authors:
  - family-names: Kelly-Reif
    given-names: Chelsea
# `version` mirrors the in-development version in pyproject.toml, which is the
# single source of truth for it; tests/test_release_metadata.py holds the two
# together.
#
# `date-released` is deliberately omitted, and its absence is checked. There is
# no `git tag` and no release in this repository. This file read
# `date-released: "2026-08-18"  # bump on every tagged release`, beside a
# CHANGELOG heading calling itself the "first tagged release" on the same date,
# and both described something that never happened (corrected 2026-08-29; see
# CHANGELOG.md `## [0.1.0]`). Add `date-released` back only once a version is
# actually tagged, which `.github/workflows/release.yml` requires to be a
# signed tag.
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
